   $q$A triangle has angles of $35^\circ$ and $65^\circ$, and the side between those two angles is 8 cm long. How many different triangles fit these conditions?$q$, $q$[{"text":"More than one, because the other sides are not given","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"thought-other-sides-can-vary"},{"text":"More than one, because the third angle could be any size","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"forgot-third-angle-is-fixed"},{"text":"None, because the angles do not add to $180^\\circ$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"expected-two-angles-to-sum-to-180"},{"text":"Exactly one, because the side and the two angles at its ends lock the triangle","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Exactly one, because the side and the two angles at its ends lock the triangle$q$, $q$Drawing the 8 cm side and the two angles at its ends makes the other two sides cross at just one point, so there is exactly one triangle with a third angle of $180 - 35 - 65 = 80$ degrees. The two given angles only need to add to less than $180^\circ$, not exactly $180^\circ$.$q$, 'draft', null)
